Job Description 
 Build the future with us 
 Are you driven by client service, business performance and the opportunity to build strong, long-term business relationships? As a Dealer Services Consultant, you will play a key role in improving business office performance by promoting the PACT/Lean method to assigned dealers, providing tailored support and helping optimize their performance.
 This position is a great opportunity to showcase your skills and fully realize your potential within a caring and trustworthy company. Here, people and their development are at the heart of our priorities, fostering an environment that encourages collaboration and innovation.
 What you’ll accomplish with us 
 As a Dealer Services Consultant, you’ll be at the core of our mission. Here are the main responsibilities:
 Develop tailored action plans based on dealer needs and objectives, including sales targets, F&I performance, sales strategies and follow-up measures;
 Prepare and conduct dealer visits according to segmentation requirements, review performance against business plans and previous results, and identify opportunities for improvement and corrective measures;
 Build and maintain strong, long-term business relationships, act as the main point of contact for clients and provide excellent service by addressing requests, issues and outstanding claim matters;
